<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jang Bogo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 846</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jang Bogo was a Silla commander and merchant who served in the Tang army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and returned home to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> along the coasts. In 828 he founded the garrison of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheonghaejin">Cheonghaejin</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wando">Wando</a>, from which he dominated shipping and trade between Silla, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. He helped place King Sinmu on the throne in 839, but was assassinated in 846.</p></div>
